# Use Base Development Rules

All AI agents working on this project must follow the comprehensive development rules and guidelines defined in:

**📋 [ai-specs/specs/base-standards.mdc](ai-specs/specs/base-standards.mdc)**

## Key Directive

- **Single Source of Truth**: All development rules, coding standards, testing practices, and workflow requirements are maintained in `base-standards.mdc`
- **No Rule Duplication**: Do not reference or follow other rule files as authoritative when they conflict with `base-standards.mdc` — `base-standards.mdc` is the entry point; detailed rules live in the linked standards files below
- **Always Current**: `base-standards.mdc` is the actively maintained configuration — other rule files may be outdated until aligned with the Flutter/Firebase stack

## What's Included in base-standards.mdc

- **Core Principles**: Small tasks one at a time, Test-Driven Development (TDD), Dart type safety, clear naming, incremental changes, Clean Architecture layer boundaries, Firebase-only data access
- **Language Standards**: English for code and comments; Spanish for documentation, commits, and PR descriptions
- **Specific Standards**: Links to detailed standards for:
  - Mobile development (Flutter, BLoC, presentation/domain Clean Architecture)
  - Firebase backend (Firestore, Authentication, datasources, Security Rules)
  - Documentation (structure, formatting, maintenance)

## Compliance

Before starting any development work, agents must:

1. Read and understand all rules in `base-standards.mdc`
2. Follow the TDD process and core principles defined there
3. Use the specified tools and testing frameworks (`flutter test`, `bloc_test`, Firebase emulators when applicable)
4. Maintain the required code quality and Dart analysis standards (`flutter analyze`)
5. Refer to the linked standards documents (`mobile-standards.mdc`, `firebase-standards.mdc`, `documentation-standards.mdc`) for detailed guidelines

**Remember**: `base-standards.mdc` is the complete development rulebook entry point for this project.
